verses.text:
as the book of the sayings of Isaiah the prophet has it:{f}
“The voice of one who calls aloud in the desert:
‘Make ready the road for the Lord;
straighten his paths.

Every ravine will be filled in,
every mountain and hill made low;
the winding ways will be straightened,
and the rough roads made level;

They resemble children who sit in the marketplace and call out to each other, saying,
‘We piped for you, but you would not dance;
we wailed, but you would not weep.’

He told them, “Whenever you pray, say:
Father,{a} may your name be held holy;
may your kingdom come.

and pardon our sins,
since we also release all who owe us;
and bring us not into testing.”{c}

saying,
“Blessed is the King who comes in the name of the Lord!{g}
In heaven peace, and glory in the highest!”

But he looked straight at them and said, “What then is this that is written:
‘The stone that the builders rejected,
this has become the cornerstone’?{a}
